       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg is double the FDA-labeled maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses above 10 mg add more side effects, such as peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nPlease check whether this is what you meant. Here are the options:\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual maximum dose. The usual start is 5 mg daily, or 2.5 mg for frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a standard starting dose if the patient is new to the drug.\n- **A second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling the patient's blood pressure, adding an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is the usual next step.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg, for example because of a specific clinical reason your attending has approved, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. I'd confirm it with your resident, attending, or pharmacist first.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
     ],
